# Keep agent rules current

On **every** user request, after finishing the work (or when discovering lasting project facts mid-task):

1. Check whether `.cursor/rules/` is still accurate for what just changed or was learned.
2. If yes and nothing durable changed → do nothing to rules.
3. If something future agents need → **update the rules in the same turn**.

## Update when

- Stack, scripts, ports, package manager, or folder layout changes
- New Tauri commands, plugins, capabilities, or IPC patterns appear
- Conventions, architecture decisions, or “gotchas” are established
- Existing rule content becomes wrong or incomplete

## How

- Prefer editing the relevant `.mdc` under `.cursor/rules/` (e.g. `foxinal-tauri.mdc`)
- Add a new focused rule only if the topic is distinct and will recur
- Keep rules concise, actionable, and under ~50 lines per file when possible
- Do not invent product requirements; only record facts useful for future agents
- Mention rule updates briefly in the reply when you change them
